menu "MIDI Clock Slave"

config AMYSYNTH_MIDI_CLOCK_SLAVE
    bool "Follow external MIDI Clock (slave mode)"
    default n
    help
        When a master (DAW, drum machine, or a MIDI keyboard) sends a
        running MIDI timing clock on the DIN port or via BLE MIDI, the
        sequencer locks its tempo to the master instead of the internal
        BPM. The inter-tick interval (24 ticks per quarter note) is
        EMA-smoothed and fits the sequencer's BPM range (40..300).

        Song start/continue (0xFA / 0xFB) and stop (0xFC) drive the local
        transport, but only while a live clock stream has been seen, so a
        keyboard that never sends clock cannot hijack the transport.

        Disabled by default so the stock devkit behaviour is unchanged;
        the board enables it in sdkconfig.defaults.

        Tempo lock only - song position pointer (0xF2) and sample-accurate
        re-phase of the sequencer steps are not implemented.

endmenu